{
  "id": 497491121,
  "iid": 25453,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "HTTP: Add expert warnings for malformed header syntax",
  "description": "## Summary\n\nThis change adds expert warnings for two malformed HTTP header cases that are currently not highlighted clearly:\n\n* Whitespace before the header field colon (for example, `Content-Length : 5`)\n* Embedded NUL bytes in HTTP header values (for example, `X-Test: abc\\0def`)\n\nThese kinds of malformed headers can be useful to spot during protocol analysis, especially when different HTTP implementations may handle them differently.\n\n## Changes\n\n* Added a new expert warning, `http.header_name.trailing_whitespace`, for header names that contain whitespace immediately before the colon.\n* Added a new expert warning, `http.header_value.invalid_nul_char`, for header values containing embedded NUL bytes.\n* Added a regression test covering both cases.\n\n## Testing\n\n* Built Wireshark and verified the changes compile successfully.\n* Verified both expert warnings are generated for malformed HTTP headers.\n* Added and verified a regression test to ensure the warnings continue to be generated.",
  "state": "merged",
