      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3475621309,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It's not necessarily wrong to spot _Control characters_ in header values, however that's not always invalid as well. The HTTP grammar is subject to change, and there's also that almost undocumented 0.9 version which would end with a somewhat tolerant interpretation.\n\n\n```\n   The backslash character (\"\\\") MAY be used as a single-character\n   quoting mechanism only within quoted-string and comment constructs.\n\n       quoted-pair    = \"\\\" CHAR\n\nCHAR           = <any US-ASCII character (octets 0 - 127)>\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6797213/avatar.png?v=1788683370",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/eugene.adell"
